# Richtext editor setup (Slate)

# Introduction
This guide shows how to add a Slate rich-text editor and integrate it into a codebase. It covers installation, a simple renderer example, and notes for switching between Slate and Lexical.
### Why Use a Rich Text Editor?
A Rich Text Editor makes writing and formatting easier because:
*   **Better Readability:** You can use headings, bold, italics, and lists to make content easier to follow.
*   **Media Support:** Easily add images, YouTube videos, and links.
*   **User-Friendly:** The editor is simple to use and works like a word processor.
*   **Consistent Formatting:** Ensures all content looks uniform across the site.
### Features of the Rich Text Editor
The Rich Text Editor in Payload CMS includes:
*   **Headings:** H1 - H6 for organizing content
*   **Lists:** Bullet points and numbered lists
*   **Media:** Embed YouTube videos and upload images
*   **Links:** Add clickable links to websites or pages
*   **Text Styling:** Bold, italics, and blockquotes
*   **Spacing:** Adds clear gaps between elements for better layout
# Installation

**Step 1:**
Install the Slate rich-text package. Run this in the repository root:

```plain
pnpm install @payloadcms/richtext-slate
```

**Step 2:**
After installing, update the CMS field configuration (for example, `payload.config.ts` under `backend/src/`).

Add or update the editor import:

```typescript
import { slateEditor } from '@payloadcms/richtext-slate'
```

If the project previously used Lexical, remove the `@payloadcms/richtext-lexical` import and replace the editor factory where appropriate. For example:

```ts
// before (Lexical)
editor: lexicalEditor(),

// after (Slate)
editor: slateEditor({}),
```

Remove any now-unused imports as needed.

**Step 3:**
Create the necessary folders and renderer components in the frontend (examples below).

**Step 4:**
Code for "**button.svelte"**

```typescript
<script lang="ts">
	export let label: string;
	export let href: string;
	export let target: string = '';
	export let transparant: boolean = false;
</script>

<a {href} {target} class="button {transparant ? 'transparant' : ''}">
	{label}
</a>

<style>
	.button {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 8px 16px;
		background-color: #007acc;
		color: white;
		text-decoration: none;
		border-radius: 4px;
		transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
	}

	.button:hover {
		background-color: #005fa3;
	}

	/* Transparent style */
	.button.transparant {
		background-color: transparent;
		border: 1px solid #007acc;
		color: #007acc;
	}

	.button.transparant:hover {
		background-color: rgba(0, 122, 204, 0.1);
	}
</style>
```

**Step 5:**
Code for "**link.svelte**"

```typescript
<script lang="ts">
	import Button from '../button/button.svelte';

	let { content } = $props();
</script>

{#if content?.children[0]?.text !== ''}
	{#if content?.fields?.style === 'default'}
		<Button
			label={content?.children[0]?.text}
			href={content?.doc?.value?.url ?? content?.url}
			target={content?.newTab ? '_blank' : undefined}
		/>
	{:else if content?.fields?.style === 'transparent'}
		<Button
			label={content?.children[0]?.text}
			href={content?.doc?.value?.url ?? content?.url}
			target={content?.newTab ? '_blank' : undefined}
			transparant={true}
		/>
	{:else if content?.linkType === 'internal'}
		<a
			class="text-alternate inline font-bold underline hover:no-underline"
			href={content?.doc?.value?.url}
			target={content?.newTab ? '_blank' : ''}
			>{content?.children?.[0]?.text}
		</a>
	{:else}
		<a
			class="text-alternate inline font-bold underline hover:no-underline"
			href={content?.url}
			target={content?.newTab ? '_blank' : ''}>{content?.children?.[0]?.text}</a
		>
	{/if}
{/if}
```

**Step 6:**
Renderer example — `richText.svelte`
See the full example in [richtext-svelte.md](../../code-snippets/richtext-svelte.md)

```typescript
<script lang="ts">
	import RichTextLink from './link/link.svelte';
	interface Props {
		json?: any;
		centerContent?: boolean;
	}

	let { json = [], centerContent = false }: Props = $props();

	let parent = $derived(json);

	function textDecoration(node: any) {
		if (node.text) {
			if (node.bold) {
				return `<strong>${node.text}</strong>`;
			}
			if (node.code) {
				return `<code>${node.text}</code>`;
			}
			if (node.italic) {
				return `<em>${node.text}</em>`;
			}
			if (node.underline) {
				return `<you>${node.text}</you>`;
			}
			if (node.strikethrough) {
				return `<s>${node.text}</s>`;
			}
			return `${node.text}`;
		}
		return '';
	}
</script>

<div class={`${centerContent ? 'flex flex-col items-center text-center' : ''}`}>
	{#if (parent && typeof parent !== 'string') || (parent?.length > 0 && typeof parent !== 'string')}
		{#each parent || [] as blocks}
			{#if !blocks?.type || blocks?.type === 'p' || blocks?.type === 'blockquote'}
				<p
					class={`${blocks?.textAlign ? blocks.textAlign : ''} mt-[1rem] min-h-[20px] text-lg leading-[1.7rem] font-extralight tracking-[0.3px] break-words whitespace-pre-wrap`}
				>
					{#each blocks.children as node}
						{#if node.type === 'link'}
							<RichTextLink content={node} />
						{:else}
							{@html textDecoration(node)}
						{/if}
					{/each}
				</p>
			{:else if blocks?.type === 'h1'}
				{#each blocks?.children as node}
					{#if node?.text}
						<span class={`text-primary h1 mb-8 text-4xl font-bold ${blocks?.textAlign || ''}`}>
							{node?.text}
						</span>
					{/if}
				{/each}
			{:else if blocks?.type.match(/^h[2-6]$/)}
				{#each blocks?.children as node}
					{#if node?.text}
						<svelte:element
							this={blocks?.type}
							class={`${blocks?.textAlign ? blocks.textAlign : ''} text-primary mt-[25px] mb-[10px] font-bold`}
						>
							{node?.text}
						</svelte:element>
					{/if}
				{/each}
			{:else if blocks?.type === 'ul'}
				<ul
					class={`${blocks?.textAlign ? blocks.textAlign : ''} mb-3 list-disc pl-8 text-lg leading-[1.7rem]`}
				>
					{#if blocks?.children || blocks?.children?.length > 0}
						{#each blocks?.children as node}
							<li>
								{#if node.children || node.children?.length > 0}
									{#each node?.children as child}
										{#if child?.type === 'link'}
											<RichTextLink content={child} />
										{:else}
											{@html textDecoration(child)}
										{/if}
									{/each}
								{/if}
							</li>
						{/each}
					{/if}
				</ul>
			{:else if blocks?.type === 'ol'}
				<ol
					class={`${blocks?.textAlign ? blocks.textAlign : ''} m-0 list-decimal pl-8 font-sans text-lg leading-[1.7rem] tracking-[-0.23px]`}
				>
					{#if blocks?.children || blocks?.children?.length > 0}
						{#each blocks?.children as node}
							<li>
								{#each node?.children as child}
									{#if child?.type === 'link'}
										<RichTextLink content={child} />
									{:else}
										{@html textDecoration(child)}
									{/if}
								{/each}
							</li>
						{/each}
					{/if}
				</ol>
			{:else if blocks?.type === 'upload'}
				<img src={blocks?.value?.url} alt={blocks?.value?.filename} class="w-full" />
			{:else if blocks?.type === 'link'}
				<RichTextLink content={blocks} />
			{:else if blocks?.type === 'video'}
				{#if blocks?.source === 'youtube'}
					<iframe
						src={`https://www.youtube.com/embed/${blocks?.id}?loop=1&modestbranding=1&rel=0&showinfo=0`}
						title="Youtube"
						frameborder="0"
						allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
						allowfullscreen
						class="aspect-video w-full"
					></iframe>
				{:else if blocks?.source === 'vimeo'}
					<iframe
						src={`https://player.vimeo.com/video/${blocks?.id}`}
						title="Vimeo"
						frameborder="0"
						allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
						allowfullscreen
						class="aspect-video w-full"
					></iframe>
				{/if}
			{/if}
		{/each}
	{/if}
</div>
```

## Implementing

**Backend:**

Configure the editor in your CMS field definitions and ensure the backend serializes rich-text to the chosen state shape (Slate or Lexical).

**Frontend**

Render the stored rich-text state with a renderer component. Example usage:

```html
{#each data.items as item}
	<RichText json={item.richTextField} />
{/each}
```

